# tRPC Client Usage Guide

Core patterns for using tRPC client methods in Vue components, prioritizing
`useAsyncData` for both queries and mutations to ensure consistent SSR and state
management.

## Client Access

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { $trpc } = useNuxtApp();
</script>
```

## Data Fetching (Queries)

Always use `useAsyncData` for data fetching to benefit from Nuxt's SSR, caching,
and state management.

### Basic Query

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { $trpc } = useNuxtApp();

const { data, status, error, refresh } = await useAsyncData(
  "unique-key",
  async () => await $trpc.process.list.query(),
);
</script>
```

### Reactive Queries (with parameters)

Use `watch` or `computed` keys to automatically re-fetch when parameters change.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { $trpc } = useNuxtApp();

const processId = ref("uuid-here");

const { data: files } = await useAsyncData(
  () => `files-${processId.value}`,
  async () => await $trpc.files.list.query({ processId: processId.value }),
  { watch: [processId] },
);
</script>
```

### Parallel Queries

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { $trpc } = useNuxtApp();

const [
  { data: files, refresh: refreshFiles },
  { data: notes, refresh: refreshNotes },
] = await Promise.all([
  useAsyncData("files", async () => await $trpc.files.list.query()),
  useAsyncData("notes", async () => await $trpc.notes.list.query()),
]);
</script>
```

## Data Modification (Mutations)

Use `useAsyncData` with `immediate: false` for mutations to manage loading
states and errors consistently.

### Basic Mutation

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { $trpc } = useNuxtApp();

const { execute: createProcess, status } = await useAsyncData(
  async () => await $trpc.process.create.mutate({ name: "New Process" }),
  { immediate: false },
);

const isCreating = computed(() => status.value === "pending");

const handleSubmit = async () => {
  await createProcess();
  // refresh related queries after success
};
</script>
```

### Mutation with Dynamic Data

For forms, you can pass the data directly in the `execute` call if structured
correctly, or use a closure.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { $trpc } = useNuxtApp();
const formData = reactive({ name: "" });

const { execute: submitForm, status } = await useAsyncData(
  async () => await $trpc.process.create.mutate(formData),
  { immediate: false },
);

const handleSubmit = async () => {
  await submitForm();
};
</script>
```

## When to Use Each Method

| Method                    | Use Case                    | Features                            |
| :------------------------ | :-------------------------- | :---------------------------------- |
| `useAsyncData` (Query)    | Standard data fetching      | SSR, Caching, Reactive (via watch)  |
| `useAsyncData` (Mutation) | Form submissions / Actions  | Consistent status tracking, No SSR  |
| `$trpc.*.query()`         | One-off, non-reactive calls | Simple scripts, non-component logic |
| `$trpc.*.mutate()`        | Simple fire-and-forget      | Background tasks, simple deletes    |

## Complete Example

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const { $trpc } = useNuxtApp();

// Query: Fetch processes
const { data: processes, refresh } = await useAsyncData(
  "processes",
  async () => await $trpc.process.list.query(),
);

// Mutation: Create process
const form = reactive({ name: "" });
const { execute: createProcess, status: createStatus } = await useAsyncData(
  async () => await $trpc.process.create.mutate(form),
  { immediate: false },
);

// Mutation: Delete process
const { execute: deleteProcess } = await useAsyncData(
  async (id: string) => await $trpc.process.delete.mutate({ id }),
  { immediate: false },
);

const handleSubmit = async () => {
  await createProcess();
  await refresh();
  form.name = "";
};

const handleDelete = async (id: string) => {
  await deleteProcess(id);
  await refresh();
};
</script>

<template>
  <div>
    <UForm :state="form" @submit="handleSubmit">
      <UInput v-model="form.name" />
      <UButton type="submit" :loading="createStatus === 'pending'">
        Create
      </UButton>
    </UForm>

    <div v-for="p in processes" :key="p.id">
      {{ p.name }}
      <UButton @click="handleDelete(p.id)">Delete</UButton>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>
```
